        "original_id": "8a02d5c5-2699-564a-be5b-7fdb0001ebe9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Jennifer Nettles, Kristian Bush, Roger Taylor, Taylor Hawkins, Lisa Carver\n- Music Groups: Sugarland, Soul Miner's Daughter, Jennifer Nettles Band, Foo Fighters, Queen\n- Songs: \"Everyday America\", \"Heaven for Everyone\"\n- Organizations: Planet Rock\n\nFacts:\n- Before Sugarland was formed, Jennifer Nettles fronted the Atlanta-based bands Soul Miner's Daughter and Jennifer Nettles Band.\n- In 2005, Planet Rock listeners voted Roger Taylor the eighth-greatest drummer in classic rock history.\n- Roger Taylor was acclaimed by Foo Fighters drummer Taylor Hawkins as one of the most influential rock drummers of the 1970s and 1980s.\n- Jennifer Nettles is best known as the lead singer of the duo Sugarland alongside Kristian Bush.\n- \"Everyday America\" was written by Jennifer Nettles, Kristian Bush, and Lisa Carver.\n- \"Heaven for Everyone\" was written by Roger Taylor.",
